        raise ValueError("values must be non-empty")
    s = sorted(values)
    rank = int(p / 100 * len(s))
    return s[rank]

codex
The bug is the one-based/zero-based mismatch: nearest-rank is `ceil(p·n/100)`, while list indexing is zero-based. I’m applying that conversion and explicitly clamping the zero percentile to the first item.
